On Thursday evening at exactly half past five, I arrive at the sports club.
I go to the counter to rent a racket.
The staff there knows my name now.
"Maya, here is the racket," he says with a smile.
I thank him and walk to the court.
Sara is waiting for me there.
We start the game right away.
Today's game is very tough.
The shuttlecock flies back and forth very fast.
Sara plays very well.
Sara's smashes are very powerful.
It is Sara who gets most of the points.
Still, I do not give up at all.
When the game ends, both of us are completely exhausted.
We are sweating a lot.
Even so, we look at each other and laugh.
I return the racket at the counter.
Then I happily walk out of the club.
